# Hollowkeep's siege (docs/design/fight.md "Siege", fortress.md): the world map's castle and its approach, 148 x 120 m
# (37 x 30 chunks of 4 m at 0.125 m), -48..128 m. Team 1 (blue) defends the sanctum, the keep's ground floor; team 2
# (red) starts on the approach past the gate's ditch and wins by holding the sanctum, with no defender inside, for
# hold_seconds without a break. The defenders win when round_seconds run out. The portcullis is down; its lever is in
# the gatehouse's guardroom. The map is not sent: the server bakes it from land_map (run from the game's root), and
# every client bakes its own copy and compares the baked map's hash at the Welcome.
#   vortex_server --session=engine/tools/server/sessions/hollowkeep.session --listen 27015 --new-token
# A public test token, published with the engine and used by tests and gates; the live server never uses it
# (--new-token makes one for the players).
token = 7a3f19c2e4b80d5661a2c3e4f5061728
template = hollowkeep
seed = 1337
play_min = -70 -54
play_max = -33 -24
height = -48 128
voxel_size = 0.125
generator = land
land_map = assets/world
max_clients = 8
chunk_capacity = 0
pack_hidden = 1
mode = siege
team_spawn_1 = -212 -142
team_spawn_2 = -238 -140
min_players = 2
round_seconds = 600
hold_seconds = 30
